{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">Every component reading a Context re-renders whenever that context's value changes, even if the component only cares about one field inside it that didn't change.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Split unrelated data into separate contexts by what actually changes together, and wrap each provider's value in useMemo so an unrelated render doesn't create a new object reference.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Memoization has to be structural all the way down, an inline setter wrapper or an unstable nested value inside a memoized object defeats the optimization, and splitting contexts doesn't help a consumer that only needs a derived slice of one large, frequently-changing value.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
